# Example 12 — TADAH:RANDOM brute-force search.
#
# Pure uniform-random sampling inside the bounds. Useful for sanity
# checks: if the best loss after N random samples beats DLIB:BFGS at
# the same N, your local optimiser is getting stuck in a poor basin.
#
# TADAH:RANDOM honours `SEED` for reproducibility and evaluates the
# in-config point as eval #0 before random sweep starts.

OPTIMIZER
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB TADAH
    ALGO RANDOM
    MAXEVAL 8
    SEED 1234
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
